 {'id':'KAR-SD-F02','candidates':[],'meaning':'All18 Shadow moves/every176 explicit field are preserved, including exact text/category/type/target/function/flag ordering. Every move explicitly TotalPP0, retained because source0 is truthy and schema unsigned permits0; omitted PP would default5. Physical category0 occurs Break/Rush/Blitz; other eight damaging moves Special1; seven status category2 omitPower and default0. Priority omitted→0 for all. Bolt/Chill/Fire EffectChance10; other15 omitted→0. Every type SHADOW, suffix shadow_pkmn. Target/function text controls separate downstream registry/Move-class dispatch and is not proved by prose description.', 'control':'Move validator rejects Status+nonzero power; converts damaging+zero power toStatus with diagnostic before register. These fixed18 satisfy category/power relation. End120accuracy60; Storm95; Blast80; Bolt/Break/Chill/Fire75; Rave70; Rush55; Wave50; Blitz40; Panicaccuracy90; other17? actual complete records carry exact accuracy and are authoritative, with End60/Panic90 and remaining16 at100.', 'failure_prefix':'Per-record validation precedes duplicate check/register. Earlier registered moves persist on later failure; final Name thenDescription message hashes precede data save, not atomic.','open':'SHADOW Type/Target registry existence, all underlying battle function classes and native PP/display/item effects require named consumers. No complete battle-effect acceptance from literal text.'},
 {'id':'KAR-SD-F03','candidates':[],'meaning':'All131 ShadowPokemon records/every262 fields are preserved with every GaugeSize and ordered Moves. Each section is baseSpecies/form0, noFlags=>[], suffix empty; every GaugeSize is explicit so4000 fallback is not activated for omitted field in these records. Ordered1..4 move lists retain original allocation; magnitude1500 through20000 is data, not a new range validation promise. get_species_form tries SPECIES_form first and falls back to baseSpecies when absent; unknown returnsnil. Missing entire record still lets Pokemon.max_gauge_size return4000 and makeShadow can use available SHADOWRUSH fallback.', 'control':'Schema Species enum/optional form tuple is normalized to species/form and generatedID before register. Optional Shadow loader invokes originalload only if Data/shadow_pokemon.dat exists. An absent optional input set returns before generic clear; an existing but invalid file does not receive the same no-op guarantee.', 'failure_prefix':'Lookup validation can raise before fallback on invalid argument types. Generic register/clear and file-save failure prefixes remainF04; no whole source rejection/host load proof is inferred.','open':'Complete Species/Move reference records and native loaded graph compatibility remain separate. No guarantee every base/form has a Shadow record.'},
 {'id':'KAR-SD-F04','candidates':[],'meaning':'Generic4–68 checks OPTIONAL/existing paths before clear; then clearregistry, parses sections in supplied path order, validates, duplicatechecks, registers each, final-validates all and game_data.save. Name/Description producers for Move and all five Item message buckets happen in final validation before registry save. Shadow per-record validate splits tuple species/form, no extra final validation. These nested backup files are concrete author inputs only when explicitly selected/provided as compile paths, not auto enabled by mechanics generation merely because bytes exist.', 'control':'Explicit file suffix derives basename after baseName+underscore; items_shadow_pkmn/moves_shadow_pkmn=>shadow_pkmn,shadow_pokemon=>empty. Optional check succeeds when any path exists, then iteration still visits all supplied paths and may fail on another missing one. No multi-file all-or-nothing guarantee.', 'failure_prefix':'Clear and earlier registrations survive later parse/duplicate/callback failure; partial message bucket updates can survive later bucket/save failure. Direct save writes use already separately audited GameData/save helpers; no rollback or successful native archive creation was run.','open':'Startup complete compile selector/caches and all default/backup combinations remain bounded by independently received full source facts, not file-location assumptions.'},
 {'id':'KAR-SD-F05','candidates':[],'meaning':'RegionalDex raw212L contains sections0 with151 species and1 with256, complete order/token/line bindings in complete_regional_dex_lists. Each list has no duplicate original token. NIDORANfE/NIDORANmA spellings are deliberately preserved; parseSpecies uppercases/trims then maps uppercaseNIDORANFE/MA back to those mixedcase IDs before registrylookup, returning actual record.id or raising undefined species. Section1 deliberately includes later evolutions YANMEGA/AMBIPOM/LICKILICKY/TANGROWTH/MAMOSWINE beyond classic251; no automatic national-order rewrite.', 'control':'compile_regional_dexes localdex_lists rejects duplicate section on encounter; prep-lines are split on commas and empty tokens skipped, with parseSpecies pertoken. Final duplicate-per-list check precedes single save_data regional_dexes.dat. Zero section index is a valid truthy source value; no header-false shortcut. A gap can leave nil list and fail list.uniq rather than implicitly filled[].', 'failure_prefix':'Parse/duplicate failure leaves old saved file because final save not reached; save itself may leave write prefix as separately audited. Compiler does not clear GameTemp regional cache within this method. No current registries were actually loaded/executed.','open':'Complete actual Species identity membership/consumer DexUI/Player indexing and native save behavior require their named contributions. No reference membership granted from token count alone.'},
